{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792185400,"nonce":"zIG2tf0w21IK5H5yIkjOR06p7KU=","title":"SSA: final phi filling builds thousands of trivial phis through unsealed desugared blocks","message":"Blocks that SSA lowering creates while desugaring expressions (the merges of if_value, block_value and the like) are never sealed. When fill_incomplete_phis reads a variable for a typed-CFG phi, the walk reaches such a merge, finds it unsealed, and leaves another incomplete phi there, which the fill loop then fills in turn, reading every predecessor again. Nearly all of them turn out trivial and collapse_trivial_phis removes them.\n\nCounted on Lua nbody start-up (34 functions, temporary instrumentation): 236 phis placed by IDF, 864 before filling, 4461 after filling, 381 after collapsing, 221 live. lua$NBody$advance$9 alone (414 blocks): 385 before filling, 2684 after, 162 after collapsing, 67 live.\n\nFix: fill_incomplete_phis runs after recompute_cfg_edges, when every predecessor list is exact, so it seals every block first. A read through a merge then takes the sealed path: it resolves a trivial merge on the spot and pushes a phi only where values differ. Filling then creates 40 phis on nbody instead of about 3600; the counts after collapsing are unchanged (381, 221 live).\n\nEquivalence: HIR dumps (ZYNTAX_DUMP_HIR_DIR, warm-up off) for all 17 Lua benchmarks and 13 official files (api, nextvar, calls, locals, constructs, closure, events, bitwise, math, strings, sort, vararg, goto), ids masked and lines sorted: identical everywhere except value identity, i.e. locals and nextvar keep 30 and 35 separate undef values where one was shared, and constructs keeps a second `const 10` (and drops an unused `const false`) per module in 3201 of 13762 module dumps. Same-arm control runs are byte-identical.\n\nMac, start-up instructions, median of 3 interleaved, same binary with a switch for the old path:\n- Lua benchmarks (ZYLUA_PROFILE_STARTUP=10, warm-up off): total 11.466G -\u003e 11.334G (-1.2%); nbody -2.5%, pipeline -3.5%, records -1.3%.\n- Lua official (one start-up): math 3.098G -\u003e 2.888G (-6.8%), footprint 64.8 -\u003e 56.8 MB; nextvar -5.4%, 92.5 -\u003e 80.3 MB; locals -3.9%, 213.5 -\u003e 202.5 MB; constructs -3.3%; api -0.2%; total -3.4%.\n- Python speed kernels (ZYPY_PROFILE_STARTUP=10, warm-up off): total 101.81G -\u003e 99.93G (-1.85%); scimark kernels about -3%, pyflate -3.5%, nqueens -3.2%, chaos -2.5%; footprint flat to -2 MB.\n\nA read through a chain of merges now recurses once per merge, as the sealed path already did for typed-CFG merges; the CLIs lower on a 1 GB stack.\n\nChecked: Mac compiler 805/0, embed 266/0, Python 99/0, Lua 97/0 (conformance 46/46); NUC x86-64 compiler 805/0, Lua 97/0, 22 Python kernels match CPython, 17 Lua benchmarks match PUC Lua.","files":null}]}